 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Ich selber führe dich\" (the libretto has \"selbsten\"), \"auf uns'rer Bahn\" (the libretto has \"unsrer\"), \"Isis Glück\" without an apostrophe, \"Wir wandelten durch Feuergluthen\" with no comma after it, the old spellings \"Noth\", \"Feuergluthen\", \"muthig\" and \"Wasserfluthen\", \"aller Orten\" in two words (both as in Mozart's score), and the print's apostrophes (\"welch'\", \"dräu'n\", \"streu'n\", \"Spiel'\", \"tausendjähr'gen\"). The two Armed Men sing \"Ihr wandelt\" where Pamina and Tamino sing \"Wir wandeln\". Repeats of the music are written out as sung: \"Wir wandeln durch des Tones Macht\" twice, with \"düstre Nacht\" three times at the end, and \"Dein Ton sei Schutz in Wasserfluthen, so wie er es im Feuer war\" twice. The chorus from within the temple (sopranos, altos, tenors, basses: \"Triumph, Triumph, du edles Paar!\") is heard with the piano and has no phrases here. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
